---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
---

<Legal title="Privacy Policy">
  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <p>
    The controller within the meaning of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is Tobias Braun. Contact:
    see the <a href={withBase('imprint')}>Legal Notice</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Server log files</h2>
  <p>
    This website is purely static. It sets no cookies, uses no external fonts and loads nothing from third
    parties. When you access it, the server automatically records connection data in log files:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>IP address of the requesting device</li>
    <li>Date and time of access</li>
    <li>Name and URL of the requested file</li>
    <li>Browser and operating system used</li>
    <li>Referrer URL (previously visited page)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This data is used only to keep the website running reliably. The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR
    (legitimate interest).
  </p>

  <h2>3. Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    This website runs on a virtual private server (VPS) that I operate and administer myself. Processing takes
    place exclusively within the EU; no data is transmitted to the USA.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Analytics – Umami (self-hosted)</h2>
  <p>
    This website may use Umami for privacy-friendly reach measurement. Umami is open-source analytics software that
    I run on my own infrastructure, so no data is transmitted to an external analytics provider or other third
    parties. Umami sets no cookies and creates no cross-device user profiles. To count unique visitors, a daily,
    salted hash is computed from IP address, user agent and website; the IP address itself is not stored. Only
    aggregated, non-personal metrics are collected (e.g. page views, browser, operating system, screen size,
    country of origin).
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR (legitimate interest in anonymous usage statistics to improve the
    website). For more information, see <a href="https://umami.is/privacy">Umami's privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>5. External links</h2>
  <p>
    This website links to external websites, such as GitHub. Their operators are solely responsible for their
    content and privacy practices. By following an external link, you leave my area of responsibility.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access your stored data (Art. 15),</li>
    <li>rectify inaccurate data (Art. 16),</li>
    <li>have your data erased (Art. 17),</li>
    <li>restrict processing (Art. 18),</li>
    <li>receive your data in a portable format (Art. 20),</li>
    <li>object to processing (Art. 21).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise these rights, contact me using the details in the <a href={withBase('imprint')}>Legal Notice</a>.
    You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Status</h2>
  <p>October 2026. This privacy policy may be updated as needed to comply with legal requirements.</p>
</Legal>
